{"id": "en_avalanche_p2", "total": 60.93, "segments": [{"text": "Part two. Mark is buried alive under deep snow because his emergency rescue beacon is off.", "start": 0.0, "end": 5.04}, {"text": "Without a transmitting signal, his friends cannot track his precise location under the heavy snow pack.", "start": 5.46, "end": 9.48}, {"text": "He remembers most buried people need to be dug out within about 15 minutes to survive.", "start": 9.88, "end": 13.32}, {"text": "Panic wastes vital oxygen, so Mark stays completely calm and breathes slowly inside his small air space.", "start": 14.0, "end": 17.976}, {"text": "He keeps his hand raised high above the packed snow while he waits for urgent help.", "start": 19.02, "end": 22.22}, {"text": "Above the surface, his rescue team arrives quickly with proper gear to search the white avalanche debris.", "start": 22.78, "end": 26.58}, {"text": "One. They use an electronic beacon to scan the slide path for any hidden transmitting signals.", "start": 26.58, "end": 31.02}, {"text": "Two. They use a long metal probe to physically test the dense snow layers for solid objects.", "start": 31.52, "end": 35.58}, {"text": "Three. They use a sturdy digging shovel to rapidly clear the heavy snow away from Mark.", "start": 36.08, "end": 39.8}, {"text": "Rescuers break through the final snow layer and open a clear pathway to his trapped face.", "start": 40.34, "end": 43.84}, {"text": "Mark takes a deep breath of fresh mountain air as his friends pull him to safety.", "start": 44.32, "end": 47.54}, {"text": "Smart survival training and calm focus save lives when a dangerous winter avalanche strikes suddenly.", "start": 48.1, "end": 52.4}, {"text": "Always check your emergency gear before you step onto any steep mountain snow slope today.", "start": 52.4, "end": 56.16}, {"text": "Follow for a new scenario tomorrow.", "start": 56.58, "end": 57.78}], "words": [["Part", 0.0, 0.36], ["two.", 0.232, 0.464], ["Mark", 1.22, 1.44], ["is", 1.44, 1.6], ["